{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1518507802,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUyOTY2NDA5MjY=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2158","origin":"github"},"title":"Enhance run/rerun with the ability to record containers required for execution","message":"It is hard to autodetect if/which containers are required for the execution of an arbitrary script via `run`. We could nevertheless record such info, by having an option, such as `run --env singularity/conversion_tools`. This could be given multiple times (if multiple containers are needed) and would merely result in a run-record in the commit message that captures this information. With such info we could then allow `rerun` to obtain the necessary containers prior execution. Containers would be linked as subdatasets, hence there is no need to capture a version separately.\n\nAs discussed in #2148, the base location for containers should be configurable (i.e. `datalad.runtime.container-dir`). Using such a config layer, will also enable later restructuring of a dataset, without breaking `rerun` be invalidating `run` commit records.\n\n@kyleam What do you think?","files":null}]}